    %% Exercise 7: the access-request flow of Company Brain (phase 3), as a sequence diagram.
    %% The participants are given. Write the messages and blocks below them.
    %% Check:   python labs/20-design-driven/check_sequence.py
    %% Render:  paste into https://mermaid.live, or view this file on GitHub (it renders Mermaid).
    %%
    %% The flow, in words (everything you need is here):
    %%  - The employee sends free text ("I need admin on the prod AWS account for 2 days") to the API,
    %%    with a request_id the client generated (the same id on every retry).
    %%  - AccessService first asks RequestStore whether this request_id was already handled.
    %%  - New request: the Classifier (an LLM behind the ChatModel port, lesson 3 structured output)
    %%    turns the text into an AccessRequest with a PROPOSED route.
    %%    If the model times out or is unavailable, do not fail and do not auto-approve:
    %%    send the request to a human route (needs_manager or needs_security).
    %%  - PolicyEngine (deterministic rules from saas_access_policy.md) decides the FINAL route.
    %%    Acme's three routes: auto_approve (approved tools, read/standard seats, no customer or
    %%    financial data), needs_manager (paid seats, unlisted tools, team write access),
    %%    needs_security (admin/owner/root, production, customer or financial data, external sharing).
    %%    The strictest matching route wins.
    %%  - The decision is saved in RequestStore (audit trail).
    %%  - auto_approve: IdentityProvider (a tool port) grants the access.
    %%    The other two routes: the Approver (manager or security, via Slack) approves or rejects,
    %%    and only an approval leads to a grant.
    %%  - The employee gets a response.
    %%
    %% Mermaid reminders: A->>B: call   B-->>A: reply (dashed)   alt label / else label / end
    %%                    opt label / end   break label / end.  Avoid ";" and "#" in message text.

    actor Emp as Employee
    participant API as AccessAPI
    participant Svc as AccessService
    participant Store as RequestStore
    participant LLM as Classifier
    participant Pol as PolicyEngine
    participant Appr as Approver
    participant IdP as IdentityProvider

    Emp->>API: POST /access-requests {text}
